  "caption": "Quinn spent an hour in the shoe shop, got told \"you over-pronate\", and bought the chunkiest pair available, certain they were injury-proof.\n\nResearch hasn't shown that any one shoe type clearly prevents running injuries. Training load errors, like doing too much too soon, tend to matter far more. Pronation doesn't always need to be \"corrected\".\n\nWhat can help: choose shoes that feel comfortable, change shoe types gradually, consider rotating two pairs, save carbon racers for key sessions, replace worn-out shoes, and build running load sensibly with strength work twice a week.\n\nGet it checked if new aches appear after a shoe change, or pain persists even after easing your training.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
